# Harness cases

## Complete programs

```flow
function main() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
```

A declaration needs no entry point.

```flow
struct Point {
    x: i32,
    y: i32
}
```

## Fragments

### Statements

```flow
let mut total: i32 = 0
total = total + 1
```

```flow
println(1)
```

### Prose shaped like code

```flow
angle evolves as velocity
```

```flow
state angle
state velocity
```

```flow
continuous
every 1 ms
```

```flow
length + voltage
```

```flow
if true {
    continuous
    every 1 ms
}
```

```flow
# just a comment, nothing else
```

```flow
function f() -> i32 {
    return undefined_thing
}
```

## Source expanders

```flow
dsys plant {
    discrete
    dt 0.1
    n 2 m 1 p 1
}
```

## Tags

```flow ignore="vision sketch"
total gibberish {{{
```

```flow expect-error
let x: i32 = {{{
```

```flow expect-error
function main() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
```

```flow expect-error
import "../../../../lib/verify/nat.flow"
```

```flow no-harness
let mut n: i32 = 1
n = n + 1
```

## Declarations, then statements

```flow
struct Point {
    x: i32
}

let p: Point = Point { x: 1 }
println(p.x)
```

## Module statics

```flow
let answer: i32 = 42
println(answer)
```

```flow
let mut counter = 0
```

## Repeated blocks

```flow
let mut a: i32 = 1
```

Text between.

```flow
let mut a: i32 = 1
```

## Broken

```flow
function f( -> i32 {
```

## from=

```flow from=prog.flow
function main() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
```

```flow from=prog.flow
function renamed() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
```

```flow from=nope.flow
function main() -> i32 { return 0 }
```

## preamble=

```flow preamble=ctx.flow
function first_value(s: Sample) -> f64 {
    return s.value
}
```

```flow preamble=ctx.flow
let s: Sample = Sample { value: 1.0 }
```

```flow preamble=nope.flow
function main() -> i32 {
    return 0
}
```

## uses= and id=

```flow uses=later
function g() -> i32 { return 0 }
```

```flow id=later
struct S { x: i32 }
```

```flow id=types
struct P { x: i32 }
```

```flow uses=types
function h(p: P) -> i32 { return p.x }
```

```flow id=s
let total: i32 = 7
```

```flow uses=s
let doubled: i32 = total * 2
```

```flow id=a
struct A { x: i32 }
```

```flow id=b
function make_a() -> A { return A { x: 1 } }
```

```flow uses=a,b
let v: A = make_a()
println(v.x)
```

```flow uses=gone
let q: i32 = 1
```
